BT /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 717 Tm (2. Purpose and scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 700 Tm (2.1 This standard sets how the Bank grants, reviews and removes access to its systems, so that each) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 686.5 Tm (person holds only the access their role needs, and no longer than they need it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 668 Tm (2.2 It applies to every account on every Bank system, held by employees, contractors and third parties.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 649.5 Tm (2.3 It applies to every platform the Bank runs, including the core banking database, the payments) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 636 Tm (gateway, the customer channels, the data warehouse, the directory and servers, the network devices and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 622.5 Tm (the cloud hosting platform.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 604 Tm (2.4 The Chief Information Security Officer owns this standard. Each platform owner applies it on their) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 590.5 Tm (platform.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 40 Tm (Access management standard, version 4.0 - page 2 of 8) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
